{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Re-check score properties",
  "description": "The scoring rules have monotonicity guarantees that the graveyard map and the ranking rely on.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "src/core/score.ts"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "src/core/score.ts changed. Run `npx vitest run test/score.test.ts`. If a property fails, report the shrunk counterexample and which guarantee broke (bounds, advisories never lower risk, time never lowers risk, usage never lowers risk, deprecated/archived always zombie, every factor has a reason). Fix the scoring, not the property, unless the property itself is wrong; explain your reasoning."
  }
}
